# Mutation efficacy per package: the share of mutants the tests kill, of the ones they could.
#
# A floor is where the package is today, and it may only move up — same rule as .coveragefloors.
# A package not listed here is reported and not enforced, because a floor invented before the
# first measurement is a number nobody chose.
#
# Efficacy answers the question coverage cannot: the line ran, but would a test have failed if it
# were wrong? `internal/control` at 68% means a third of the mutations in its covered code are
# invisible to its unit tests.
internal/control  75
